{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFYRNg8XhdiZB2WPnr2w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] No file in the package mentions `Ornith-1.0-35B`\n\nThe `code` tier now offers `ornith-ai/Ornith-1.5-35B-A3B-Turbo` (54% NPU, 262144 context) where it offered `deepreinforce-ai/Ornith-1.0-35B`, as the first fallback after `Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B`, which is still the default. All 6 tests in `npm test` pass, and everything is committed in two commits.\n\n1. **Tier table (`1f548e4`):** a one-line change in `tiiny-router/tiers.py`. I added two tests to `test/test_installed_tree.py` that run `route_check.py` from a copy of the tree. They read the `code` rows from `--all` and check the default, the new fallback with its NPU share and context, and that 1.0 is gone (also checked in `--tier code --alternatives`). Both failed before the change and pass after it.\n2. **`thinking.py`:** checked, no change needed. It has no per-model table and reads each model's reasoning settings from the device at runtime.\n3. **Docs (`1cec51b`):** replaced 1.0 in `SKILL.md`, both places in `references/backend.md` (tier table and the `tiiny` provider `models:` block with `context_length: 262144`), `docs/PATTERN.md`, `docs/README.md` and `docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md`. The README description now covers 1.5 (mixture-of-experts, about 3B of 35B active, built for repository-scale coding and agentic work). I removed the 1.0 entry from the two-box capability matrix. I didn't write a test for this item, because a test that greps doc text would be brittle; I checked with a grep instead. The only remaining mention is in the test that checks 1.0 is absent.\n4. **`AGENTS.md`:** added a short \"Changing a tier model\" section listing the files that repeat the tier table by hand.\n\nThree things you may want to decide on, also recorded in `.redeye/notes.md`:\n\n- **Reasoning column conflict:** the ticket calls 1.0's reasoning \"always on, not toggleable\", but the doc tables list it as `switch`. Since the ticket says 1.5 behaves the same as 1.0, I kept `switch` for 1.5 rather than pick a side.\n- **Download status:** I kept \"downloaded\" in `SKILL.md`'s \"On the device?\" column without being able to confirm it on the device.\n- **Stale ordering in docs:** the tier tables in `docs/` and `references/backend.md` still put `Qwen3-Coder-30B` first in the `code` tier, unlike `tiers.py`. That was already the case before this ticket, so I left it alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":163,"cache_read_input_tokens":68184,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":163},"output_tokens":794,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e049b101-1de2-4d7e-adb4-fac63c077fc4","uuid":"567e3619-a1de-41dc-8ba4-61e25231f28a","timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:44:49.463Z","request_id":"req_011ChFYRNVTktF6mshonDY7h"}
